# Generated from: specs/46-final-production-launch-gate/requirements.md
Feature: Final production launch gate
  As a project owner
  I want one operational release gate for the final production launch
  So that the delivered #13-#22 workflows are proven safely before any public host is exposed

  @SCN001
  Scenario: Closed prerequisite set keeps the release at VERSION 0.13.0
    Given issues #13 through #22 are closed
    And the repository root VERSION is 0.13.0
    And no public host is retained or exposed
    When the final launch gate is prepared
    Then the evidence records the closed prerequisite set
    And VERSION remains exactly 0.13.0
    And no product implementation or enhancement is introduced

  @SCN002
  Scenario: Actual Railway project is imported without destructive drift
    Given the linked Railway project is the intended production project
    When the owner imports it into the approved TypeScript IaC representation and previews the plan
    Then the live resource identities and non-secret configuration are reconciled
    And the plan contains no unreviewed delete or replace operation
    And no secret value is present in the IaC source, plan, logs, or evidence
    And no public host is created or advertised during import or planning

  @SCN003
  Scenario: Production admission runs the exact migration predeploy
    Given an immutable production candidate has passed non-destructive IaC review
    When deployment admission evaluates the candidate
    Then the platform runs dotnet VolunteerCoordinator.Web.dll --migrate-only exactly once before the serving process
    And the migrate-only process exits successfully without binding an HTTP port
    And /health/ready reports database-aware readiness before serving traffic
    And ordinary Web startup and public requests do not apply migrations

  @SCN004
  Scenario: Migration or readiness failure blocks serving traffic
    Given the candidate migration or database-aware readiness check fails
    When the platform evaluates deployment admission
    Then the candidate is not made public
    And the failure is recorded as a blocking gate result

  @SCN005
  Scenario: Public deployment and rollback preserve the authoritative service
    Given IaC, migration, and readiness admission have passed
    When the owner deploys the candidate and exercises rollback to the last known-good release
    Then the public host is exposed only after admission
    And the deployment and rollback identities are recorded without secrets
    And the rolled-back service becomes healthy without destructive database or workflow-state rewriting

  @SCN006
  Scenario: Daily backup meets RPO and restores in isolation
    Given production PostgreSQL contains authoritative schedule and workflow state
    When the owner verifies backup and recovery operations
    Then the observed recovery point is no older than 24 hours
    And a selected backup restores to an isolated PostgreSQL target
    And integrity checks and representative schedule, request, assignment, audit, notification, and privacy reads pass
    And the restored target is not attached to public serving

  @SCN007
  Scenario: Two independent production coordinators complete handoff
    Given production OIDC and the protected application allowlist are configured
    When two independent coordinators authenticate in separate sessions
    Then both can perform authorized coordinator workflows and produce distinct audit identities
    And an unallowlisted identity is denied
    When the outgoing coordinator is removed through the protected handoff
    Then the remaining and replacement coordinators continue without shared credentials or schedule loss
    And no OIDC secret or raw session/capability material is exposed

  @SCN008
  Scenario: Real Resend sandbox covers every template and signed outcome
    Given the verified sandbox sender, reserved test recipient, and protected Resend credentials are available
    When the owner sends every delivered #18/#19 notification and recovery template
    Then each template records a provider message ID and safe visible state
    When signed delivered, bounced, and complained events are received
    Then raw-body authentication, deduplication, out-of-order handling, and safe monotonic state transitions pass
    And no raw webhook body, credential, recipient secret, or raw link is retained in evidence

  @SCN009
  Scenario Outline: Real Resend failures use bounded absolute retry and idempotency
    Given a sandbox notification is eligible for delivery
    When the provider produces a <failure> outcome
    Then the application records the safe failure category without rolling back workflow state
    And transient outcomes follow the absolute 0, 1, 5, 30, and 120 minute schedule where applicable
    And an identical in-memory payload reuses its idempotency key only within the approved window
    And fresh materialized attempts use a new idempotency key

    Examples:
      | failure  |
      | timeout  |
      | HTTP 429 |
      | HTTP 5xx |
      | permanent failure |

  @SCN010
  Scenario: Recovery and both access reissue modes work in the real sandbox
    Given a test volunteer has a delivered accountless capability
    When the volunteer completes recovery and redeems the replacement capability
    Then the current hub state and one-time action behavior are correct
    When a coordinator sends ordinary replacement access and then revoke-now replacement access
    Then earlier capabilities follow the approved invalidation policy
    And each replacement is audited and safely delivered or visibly failed
    And secret and raw-link scans find no unsafe output or persistence

  @SCN011
  Scenario: Untrained desktop and mobile smoke covers delivered workflows
    Given admission has passed and controlled test data is available
    When an untrained operator and test volunteer exercise delivered #13-#22 workflows on desktop and narrow mobile surfaces
    Then setup, publication, local-time and recurring schedules, approval/direct claim, recurring commitments, exceptions, action-hub recovery, notifications, privacy/removal, stewardship, audit, handoff, failure, retry, and revocation paths are reachable
    And each journey has a clear next step without technical training
    And routine surfaces do not expose raw identifiers, provider terminology, secrets, JSON, UTC-only explanations, or raw links

  @SCN012
  Scenario: Final privacy security and query-budget gates block unsafe launch
    Given the candidate and non-secret operational evidence are available
    When the owner runs privacy, retention, security, dependency/image/configuration, authorization, webhook, token, and representative query-budget checks
    Then every named check passes with a command or observable result
    And sensitive material is absent from source, configuration, logs, audit, persistence, image layers, and evidence
    And bounded coordinator queries remain within the approved budget
    And any failed check blocks launch acceptance
